    "@value" : "threat event type"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A description of a kind of event that, if it occurred, could adversely affect assets, such as credential phishing, ransomware encryption or a server-room fire."
  }, {
    "@language" : "fr",
    "@value" : "Description d'un type d'événement qui, s'il se produisait, pourrait porter atteinte à des actifs, comme l'hameçonnage d'identifiants, le chiffrement par rançongiciel ou l'incendie d'une salle des serveurs."
  } ],
  "https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000283" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000069"
  } ],
  "https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000284" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000064"
  } ],
  "https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000285" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Possible events are described, not instantiated (Phase 1 section 5.3); linked to ATT&CK by mapping."
  } ],
  "https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000286" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "NIST SP 800-30 Rev. 1 (2012), Appendices D-I (threat sources, events, vulnerabilities and predisposing conditions, likelihood, impact, risk)"
  }, {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Phase 1 report (8 Oct 2026), section 5 and recorded decisions"
  } ],
